with the new air pots Pro it seems like  Apple is attacking every single thing  that people complained about with the  original air pods so in this review  we'll see if Apple succeeded let me  first remind you of the main problems  people had with the air pots  first off quite a few people have ear  canals that simply don't fit the air  pods like my brother-in-law Ben who  absolutely loves Apple products but air  pods just won't fit in his ears a lot of  people also felt that the sound quality  of the air pods was lacking for the  price especially the bass reproduction  and people didn't really like the  long-stem design in fact they still say  it looks like a toothbrush hanging out  of your ear there were also connection  and lag issues which thankfully were  fixed with air pots to in its new h1  chip which is the same chip that's also  packed into the pros so that's fixed  people complained about no noise  cancellation and since the older air  pods don't have a seal design there's  already a lot of sound leakage I  personally was disappointed with the  lack of controls on the air pods being  limited to two control options and  having to double tap the air pods which  worked decently well but when it didn't  it was extremely annoying other than  that the air pods were always great and  very reliable becoming the best-selling  wireless earphones in the world and now  we've got the ear pods Pro so let's see  if Apple fix those issues starting with  the new design yes the new case is  larger but not large enough to make it  an inconvenience it still fits perfectly  fine in my small pocket within a pocket  so don't worry about the case at all the  new design of the air pods is definitely  different with new black vents and  details all the way around so it's  pretty easy to tell that sone is wearing  the pros and not the regular ear pods  especially since the stem has been  shortened by quite a bit making it look  a bit nicer and it also stops the stem  from rubbing against your skin if you  didn't put them in at the correct angle  I love the Apple includes three  different sizes of silicone ear tips and  they even have an ear tip fit test to  make sure they seal well but I'd  recommend trying all of them out because  we got better bass with the largest tips  even though the median ones pass a test  Apple has done something truly  YOUnique with these silicone tips almost  every single in ear earphone I've ever  used has a thin protruding plastic tube  for the speakers that actually goes into  your ear canal alongside the silicone  tips and not long after wearing  earphones like that my ears would start  to hurt from the plastic insert and  that's part of the reason why I switched  to Apple earpods  many years ago but with the pros the  speaker grille is actually flush with  the pro itself so only the soft silicone  tip goes into your ear that means your  ears literally won't hurt at all even  after hours of use and even better the  tips include their own little plastic  grille so ear wax or anything else will  never get into the actual speaker grille  itself unlike the original ear pods  which were really annoying to clean and  could actually lower the sound quality  so with the air pod pros just take off  the silicone tip rinse it dry it and  it's perfectly clean and because of this  design it allows the pros to have a  massive speaker grille especially  compared to other recently released in  ear earphones which makes it much easier  to recreate a wide soundstage of  frequencies the air pod pros feature of  vents on the outside that lets an air so  that the pressure inside your ears  actually matches the pressure of the  outside world so even though they're  using a sealed in ear design they don't  plug your ears like basically every  other in ear earphone does so they feel  just as free and comfortable as they did  before almost like they're not even  there it's seriously the best of both  worlds and you really have to try it for  yourself to understand how great this  feature is the pros also have a new  force touch sensor that replaces the old  double tap design for controls and so  far I'm extremely happy with the change  its accurately registered in my presses  every single time so far and it's super  sensitive and quick with no lag time in  an audible click each time you press so  it's much more reliable than the double  tap method I especially like that you  have so many more options now allowing  you to play and pause skip forward skip  back and switch between noise  cancellation modes all on one air pod  pro with the original air pods you  literally had to pick and choose just  one control for each side and to make it  even better you can go into your  bluetooth  settings on your iPhone tap the I icon  next to your air pod pros and  individually change the press and hold  commands for each side now before I get  into sound quality I want to talk about  noise cancellation if you've never tried  it before  it'll literally blow your mind when you  turn it on any background noise like the  air conditioning just disappears with  the old air pods I'd have to max out the  volume to drown out any background noise  but then basically everyone around you  can hear what you're listening to what's  great about the noise cancellation is  that it now allows you to listen to  music at much lower volumes while in  noisy environments and the transparency  mode is amazing it uses the microphone  to basically record your surroundings  and then the speakers play all of it  directly into your ears Apple absolutely  nailed it with the volume balanced in  this mode because with it on like it is  right now you can actually forget that  you're wearing them and in terms of how  well the noise reduction works larger  over the ear headphones like the Sony WH  1000 m3s do a better job because they  obviously have much more power so in the  past you definitely want to take those  with you onto an airplane while  traveling but to be completely honest  the noise reduction on the air pod pros  are more than good enough to be able to  leave those large Sony's behind in a big  surprise to me was that the pros  actually have better sound quality than  those 350 dollar Sony's now they're not  as loud or as Spacey but the quality  itself is actually better and it's  noticeably better compared to the old  airport the dynamic range or separation  of low medium and high frequencies  improved over the air pods too you can  easily hear and distinguish every  instrument nothing gets blended together  like you get with a lot of other  earphones out there the bass now feels  very deep rich and accurate compared to  before in vocal reproduction is  incredibly clear along with bright highs  that no longer sound blaringly loud  tinny or distorted at maximum volume and  that's because of the inward-facing  microphone that literally listens for  distortion and automatically reaches the  frequencies of the sound to make sure  that there is no distortion and even  though it does this the pros are still  more than loud enough especially with  the added noise reduction  there's  songs that I used to play that have very  specific high notes that would always  make my speakers distort like the song  strobe by deadmau5 so I replayed those  songs on the air pod pros and it  actually tuned those frequencies to get  rid of the distortion that's just insane  the best and my favorite part about this  feature is that two years down the line  when other earphones will usually  degrade in quality and start distorting  at high volumes the air pot pros  shouldn't the inward-facing microphone  is also used for the new adaptive EQ  feature which analyzes how the sound  bounces off the inside of your ear canal  and then Tunes it to the specific shape  of your ear sort of like how sound  engineers tune the sound in IMAX movie  theatres to the shape of the theater  room to make sure it sounds amazing for  the audience so Apple is using this  incredible software combined with three  different sizes of ear tips to make sure  that each and every person experiences  awesome sound quality no matter how big  or oddly shaped their ear canals are  with all that said I can safely say that  yes Apple actually fixed basically every  major issue that people had with the  original ear pods and they added a bunch  of awesome new features like noise  cancellation and ipx4 sweat and water  resistance so if you're still trying to  figure out if spending the extra cash on  the air Potts Pro is worth it over the  air pods - I would say that if there's  any way possible that you can stretch  your budget enough to get the air pods  pro do it by them and never look back  because I honestly think that Apple has  absolutely nailed it with the air pods  pro if you enjoy this review tap the  like button and check out the air paws  Pro versus air pods - full comparison  video right over there and if you're not  already soft click that circle above  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

